<!--
    Device VINTF manifest, taken from itel stock revision 28
    (/vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml) rather than left to the build to
    generate.

    The generated manifest describes only the HALs the ROM builds from source.
    Every MediaTek / Transsion / NXP / Trustonic HAL on this device ships as a
    prebuilt, so a generated manifest declares almost none of them. The one
    that bit us in practice was thermal: without the entry below,
    android.hardware.thermal@2.0-service.mtk cannot register with
    hwservicemanager, init respawns it about every five seconds forever, and
    `dumpsys thermalservice` reports "HAL Ready: false".

    Stock's own manifest.xml has the thermal entry, and both versions of it —
    @1.0 and @2.0 — which is what the service's .rc actually advertises. Taking
    the file whole is therefore both the accurate description of this device
    and the fix.

    Per-service fragments under /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/ ship alongside
    their own blobs and are merged with this file at runtime; they are not
    reproduced here.

    Header from the stock assemble_vintf run removed — it listed that build's
    input fragment names, which mean nothing in this tree.
-->
