    <!-- Restored from stock 2026-08-11. Without this the sensors HAL cannot
         register AT ALL, and aborts every 5s forever:

           mtkSubHal: HIDL mediatek subhal 2.x load sensor module success.
           hwservicemanager: Cannot find entry
             android.hardware.sensors@2.0::ISensors/default in either framework
             or device VINTF manifest
           Failed to register Sensors HAL instance
           ... SIGABRT, 'terminating'   x31 in one boot

         Note the sub-HAL loads fine. HIDL simply refuses to register a service
         VINTF does not declare, so this is an implementation with no
         declaration: the exact inverse of the media.c2 defect, where VINTF
         declared a HAL nothing could provide. (No "- -" without a space in an
         XML comment, incidentally; that is illegal and will not parse.)

         How it went missing: this file is stock's manifest, and stock declares
         sensors@2.0 here. Our copy had lost it (along with boot@1.0 and
         composer@2.1, which survive only because fragments declare their newer
         minor versions @1.2 and @2.3, and HIDL minor versions are backward
         compatible). Sensors had no such cover: its only other declaration was
         android.hardware.sensors@2.1-multihal.xml, one of the 16 FINAL12
         fragments the provenance audit correctly deleted. The cleanup was right
         and it removed the last thing declaring this HAL.

         We ship stock's own service binary for it,
         android.hardware.sensors@2.0-service.multihal-mediatek, so @2.0 is the
         correct version to declare. -->
    <hal format="hidl">
        <name>android.hardware.sensors</name>
        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
        <version>2.0</version>
        <interface>
            <name>ISensors</name>
            <instance>default</instance>
        </interface>
        <fqname>@2.0::ISensors/default</fqname>
    </hal>
